MOTION STUDIO — ADDITIONAL NOTICE

Motion Studio is made publicly available for learning, experimentation,
personal projects, collaboration, modification, contribution, and other
non-commercial purposes under the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0.

You may use, study, run, modify, fork, and redistribute Motion Studio
only as permitted by the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0.

COMMERCIAL USE

The standard license does not authorize commercial use of Motion Studio.

If you intend to commercially exploit Motion Studio, including but not
limited to:

- selling Motion Studio;
- selling a modified version or fork;
- offering Motion Studio as a paid SaaS;
- creating a paid white-label version;
- commercially redistributing Motion Studio;
- licensing a derivative version for payment;
- incorporating substantial portions of Motion Studio into a commercial
  product or service;
- charging specifically for access to functionality substantially
  provided by Motion Studio;

you must first contact the Motion Studio copyright holders and obtain
separate written authorization.

Contacting the maintainers does not automatically grant commercial rights.

Commercial authorization is valid only when expressly granted in writing
by the applicable copyright holders.


ATTRIBUTION

Original Motion Studio attribution must be preserved.

Copies, forks, modifications, and redistributions must retain all applicable:

- copyright notices;
- author notices;
- contributor notices;
- license notices;
- Required Notice lines;
- NOTICE files;
- attribution comments;
- third-party copyright notices;
- third-party license notices.

You may identify yourself as the author of your own modifications.

You may not remove or conceal the original Motion Studio authorship or
represent the original Motion Studio source code as your own work.

Modified versions must clearly state that they are based on Motion Studio.

Forks and derivative projects must not falsely represent themselves as
the official Motion Studio project or imply endorsement by the original
Motion Studio maintainers without authorization.


